#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from Sampler to Executor {#migrate-from-sampler-to-executor}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide describes how to move quantum sampling workloads from the IBM Quantum&reg; Sampler\n"
"primitive to the Executor primitive.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Beta release\">\n"
"The Executor primitive is part of the\n"
"[directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model). All components in the directed execution model are currently in beta and might not be stable. You are invited to test them and provide feedback by opening an issue in the [Samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic/issues) or [qiskit-ibm-runtime](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/issues) GitHub repositories.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Should you migrate? {#should-you-migrate}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not everyone should migrate from Sampler to Executor.  There are many differences between the primitives, but the following guidance can help you decide whether to migrate:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Migrate to Executor** if you are a quantum information scientist who runs \n"
"utility-scale experiments and needs fine-grained, reproducible control over\n"
"techniques like Pauli twirling, noise-model learning and injection, and basis\n"
"changes — or who needs one of the additional capabilities provided by Executor.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Continue using Sampler** if you want a simple, high-level interface and want the primitive to manage error suppression and mitigation for you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limitations and caveats {#limitations-and-caveats}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because Executor and the directed execution model are in beta, note the following before you decide to migrate:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**No simulator support yet**: Unlike Sampler, which has an `AerSampler`\n"
"implementation in [`qiskit-aer`](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-aer) for local\n"
"simulation, there is currently no simulator backend for Executor. Simulator\n"
"support is expected to arrive soon. In the meantime, you can still inspect and [sample\n"
"the template circuit locally](#sample-local) to\n"
"validate your workflow before submitting it to hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**This guide covers Sampler only, not Estimator.** Migrating from Estimator to\n"
"Executor is considerably more involved than migrating from Sampler because Estimator\n"
"computes expectation values rather than returning raw samples. Reproducing Estimator's behavior with\n"
"Executor requires additional post-processing. Utility functions to help migrate from \n"
"Estimator to Executor are still under development, so this guide\n"
"intentionally describes only the Sampler workflow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key differences between Executor and Sampler {#key-differences-between-executor-and-sampler}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sampler and Executor both sample the output registers of quantum circuits, but they\n"
"target different users:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampler** is a high-level abstraction. It has the following characteristics: \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It has built-in error suppression (dynamical decoupling and twirling).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It makes implicit decisions for you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - It is designed so algorithm developers can focus on innovation rather than data.\n"
"  conversion.\n"
"- **Executor** is part of the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model). It differs from Sampler in many ways and has the following characteristics:\n"
"  - It has no built-in error suppression or mitigation. Instead, you capture your design intent on the client\n"
"  side (by using circuit annotations and a *samplex*), and the costly generation of circuit\n"
"  variants is shifted to the server side. \n"
"  - It makes no implicit decisions. It follows your directives exactly, giving full control and transparency. \n"
"  - Executor and Samplomatic together expose additional capabilities that Sampler does not offer, including (but not limited to) the following:\n"
"    - More twirling groups: Samplomatic lets you choose which twirling group to apply\n"
"      per box, rather than being limited to the single strategy that Sampler applies for you. It also supports twirling groups other than Pauli, such as the `\"local_c1\"` twirling\n"
"      group. \n"
"    - Kerneled and classified measurements together: Setting\n"
"      `QuantumProgram.meas_level = \"both\"` (added in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.48.0) requests\n"
"      that both classified and kerneled measurements be present in the results, instead\n"
"      of picking a single measurement type per job.\n"
"    - Twirling for circuits with fractional gates: Executor can apply twirling to\n"
"      circuits that contain fractional gates.\n"
"    - Fine-grained, composable error mitigation: For example, choosing which\n"
"      circuit layers to mitigate and adjusting the noise rates injected into the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
"    - Future new capabilities are expected to be released to Executor\n"
"    first and might not be ported to Sampler. If you rely on access to the\n"
"    latest features, Executor is the more future-proof choice.\n"
"    - The base Qiskit package does not yet provide\n"
"a base class for the Executor primitive (it does for`SamplerV2`).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual mapping {#conceptual-mapping}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following table demonstrates how Sampler concepts map to Executor. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept                | Sampler                                   | Executor                                                        |\n"
"| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Import                 | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime import SamplerV2`| `from qiskit_ibm_runtime import Executor`                       |\n"
"| Input                  | List of [PUBs](/guides/primitive-input-output#overview-of-pubs) (tuples)                 | A `QuantumProgram` of `QuantumProgramItem` objects          |\n"
"| Circuit and parameters    | `(circuit, params, shots)` tuple          | `program.append_circuit_item(circuit, circuit_arguments=...)`   |\n"
"| Twirling | `TwirlingOptions`                      | Explicit through annotated boxes and a samplex (`append_samplex_item`) |\n"
"| Run call               | `sampler.run([pub, ...])`                 | `executor.run(program)`                                         |\n"
"| Result type            | `PrimitiveResult` of `SamplerPubResult`   | `QuantumProgramResult` (iterable)                               |\n"
"| Access data         | `result[0].data.<register>` (`BitArray`)  | `result[0][\"<register>\"]` (`np.ndarray`)                        |\n"
"| Manage noise      | Built-in options                          | Must be manually composed (annotations, samplex, `NoiseLearnerV3`)         |\n"
msgstr ""

